"Time(h)":72,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":"3.2 ± 0.4","IC50_Dark_value":3.2,"Method":"SRB","DOI":"10.1016/j.jinorgbio.2017.04.003","Year":2017,"Type":"IC50","comparison":{"compound_id":"OBMD011700","measurement_id":"MCTM-037326","value":"4.4 ± 1.7","numeric":4.4}},{"Measurement_ID":"MCTM-037327","Abbreviation_in_the_article":"[Pt(glut)(dbtp)2] 3","Cell_line":"HL-60","Time(h)":72,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":"0.3 ± 0.1","IC50_Dark_value":0.3,"Method":"MTT","DOI":"10.1016/j.jinorgbio.2017.04.003","Year":2017,"Type":"IC50","comparison":{"compound_id":"OBMD011700","measurement_id":"MCTM-037327","value":"1.2 ± 0.3","numeric":1.2}},{"Measurement_ID":"MCTM-037328","Abbreviation_in_the_article":"[Pt(glut)(dbtp)2] 3","Cell_line":"HT-29","Time(h)":72,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":"2.4 ± 0.8","IC50_Dark_value":2.4,"Method":"SRB","DOI":"10.1016/j.jinorgbio.2017.04.003","Year":2017,"Type":"IC50","comparison":{"compound_id":"OBMD011700","measurement_id":"MCTM-037328","value":"8.1 ± 1.4","numeric":8.1}},{"Measurement_ID":"MCTM-037329","Abbreviation_in_the_article":"[Pt(glut)(dbtp)2] 3","Cell_line":"OVCAR-3","Time(h)":72,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":"6.0 ± 1.6","IC50_Dark_value":6,"Method":"SRB","DOI":"10.1016/j.jinorgbio.2017.04.003","Year":2017,"Type":"IC50","comparison":{"compound_id":"OBMD011700","measurement_id":"MCTM-037329","value":"11 ± 1","numeric":11}},{"Measurement_ID":"MCTM-037330","Abbreviation_in_the_article":"[Pt(glut)(dbtp)2] 3","Cell_line":"A2780cisR","Time(h)":72,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":"2.7 ± 0.2","IC50_Dark_value":2.7,"Method":"SRB","DOI":"10.1016/j.jinorgbio.2017.04.003","Year":2017,"Type":"IC50","comparison":{"compound_id":"OBMD011700","measurement_id":"MCTM-037330","value":"11 ± 1","numeric":11}}],"logp":[{"abbreviation_in_the_article":"[Pt(glut)(dbtp)2] 3","value":2.4,"value_relation":"=","std":0.07,"type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"0.9% NaCl","doi":"10.1016/j.jinorgbio.2017.04.003","year":2017,"record_id":"MLDB-001919","detection":"UV-Vis","method_description":"The lipophilicity (logP) of the compounds was determined using shake–flask method [37]. Aqueous (0.9% w/v) sodium chloride and organic (n–octanol) phases were saturated for 1 week. Drugs were dissolved at a concentration of 0.30 mg mL- 1 in 2.5 mL of saturated n–octanol, except for cisplatin, carboplatin and complex 1 or 4 that were dissolved in the aqueous phase. An equal volume of immiscible solvent was added and the solutions were mixed mechanically in a plastic tubes for 30 min. Samples were centrifuged (6000 rpm, 15 min). After separation, the phases were analyzed by UV–Vis spectroscopy to determine the amount of the compound in each phase. The absorption values before and after shaking were compared and based on the Lambert–Beer Law, the partition coefficient in both phases for each compound was calculated to determine the logP values."}]}